  "steps": [
    "<strong>Cook the Dal Base:</strong> Rinse lentils until water runs clear. Heat oil in a large pan over medium. Soften onion 3–4 min; add garlic and ginger 1 min. Add cumin, turmeric, curry/garam masala, chilli flakes; bloom 30–45 sec. Stir in carrots.",
    "Add lentils and water/stock; bring to a boil then reduce heat. Simmer 12–15 min until carrots and lentils are soft. Stir in coconut milk (optional) and simmer 5 min. Season with salt, pepper, and finish with lemon/lime juice.",
    "<strong>Tempeh Breadcrumbs:</strong> Heat oven to 200°C / 400°F (fan). Toss crumbled tempeh with tamari, garlic granules, a little oil. Mix in breadcrumbs and seasoning. Spread on a tray; bake 12–18 min, turning halfway, until crisp and golden. (Or pan-fry until crisp.)",
    "Serve bowls of dal topped generously with the crunchy tempeh crumbs. Add extra lemon/lime or herbs."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Loosen thick dal with hot water.",
    "Boost heat with fresh chilli or extra flakes.",
    "Swap tempeh crumbs for roasted chickpeas for another protein crunch."
  ]
